When find ends, Ladybird makes an active match in a text control the
control’s selection. Chromium does the same for a match in an <input> or
a <textarea>, in TextFinder::SetFindEndstateFocusAndSelection(), and it
also focuses the control, where Ladybird leaves the focus as it was. The
report says that Firefox puts the caret at the start of the match
instead. From reading Chromium’s source.
